 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504783,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In an Internet giveaway, every 130th person who submits a survey receives $250, and every 900th person receives a free cell phone. How many submissions must be received for the first person to receive both prizes?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "\n<p>Find the LCM of 130 and 900.</p>\n<p>Find the prime factorization of each number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"255 = 2 \\times 5 \\times 13\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"900 = {2^2} \\times {3^2} \\times {5^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Make a table of each prime and the largest exponent for each prime.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exponent</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LCM is the product of each prime raised to the powers identified in the table.</p>\n<p>The LCM is <span data-math=\"{2^2} \\times {3^2} \\times {5^2} \\times 13 = 11,700\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The prize winner is the one who submits the 11,700th submission.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The first person to receive both giveaways would be the person who submits the 11,700th submission."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
